{"type": "message", "id": "bab3753a", "parentId": "d1147550", "timestamp": "2026-04-10T11:02:28.868Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "toolu_bdrk_01LvyA6gpFDrvgVurqgkN6qt", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"Eurostat railway suicide statistics Germany 2014 2020 percentage decrease\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 945,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"966e02073e573d33\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRailway safety statistics in the EU Statistics Explained\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"966e02073e573d33\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/SEPDF/cache/94376.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f44fa3ea9702bf83\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIt should be noted that there are no railways in the EU countries Cyprus and Malta, ... The number of significant railway accidents in the EU fell almost continuously between 2010 and 2020, with the · only exceptions being <strong>a sharp increase in 2014 (+6.7%)</strong> and a slight increase in 2017 (+2.1%).\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f44fa3ea9702bf83\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6074532ab738f678\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRail transport fatalities drop by 11% in 2024 - News articles - Eurostat\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6074532ab738f678\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/products-eurostat-news/w/ddn-20251216-2\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c7655b89c5d67831\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe number of suicides on railways is constantly much higher than the number of fatalities despite the downward trend seen in the EU the past decade (2 357 in 2024 compared with 2 608 in 2014, <strong>-9.6%)</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c7655b89c5d67831\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"December 16, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bd14aa3d2803c6aa\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRailway safety statistics in the EU - Statistics Explained - Eurostat\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bd14aa3d2803c6aa\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/index.php?title=Railway_safety_statistics_in_the_EU\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5a156a05cb234f3d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIt should be noted that there are no railways in the EU countries Cyprus and Malta, nor in the EEA/EFTA country Iceland. <strong>The number of significant railway accidents in the EU fell almost continuously between 2010 and 2020, with the only exceptions being a sharp increase in 2014</strong> ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5a156a05cb234f3d\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0fee2667c1eadfa9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nBehavioral and location‐related antecedents of train suicides - Moritz - 2023 - Suicide and Life-Threatening Behavior - Wiley Online Library\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0fee2667c1eadfa9\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/sltb.12941\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b414cbf8f6d0acf8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nA total of <strong>78.6% (n = 44) of the present sample were German nationals</strong>, which is somewhat lower than the proportion of individuals with German citizenship in Hamburg in 2020 (82.9%; Federal Statistical Office/Statistisches Bundesamt, 2021).\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b414cbf8f6d0acf8\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 30, 2023\",\n      \"siteName\": \"onlinelibrary.wiley.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"66da31f50e87687c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nEU railway deaths fall in 2024\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"66da31f50e87687c\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.globalrailwayreview.com/news/233725/railway-deaths-in-the-eu-fall-in-2024-after-years-of-fluctuating-trends/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5ba5c0898e672b83\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn 2024, there were 2,357 suicides, <strong>down 9.6% from 2,608 in 2014.</strong> Germany recorded the highest number with 688, followed by France with 267 and the Netherlands with 186. The lowest numbers were observed in Lithuania with none, Greece with one, ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5ba5c0898e672b83\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"December 17, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.globalrailwayreview.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"20f999e02ba7d01c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSearch results for \\\"유로컵 참가국-（H87.CC）-유로컵 참가국->>h87.cc<<-h0neo.html\\\" - Statistics Explained - Eurostat\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"20f999e02ba7d01c\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/index.php/Railway_safety_statistics_in_the_EU\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0d9b1f73f4554c3f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRetrieved from &quot;https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/index.php?title=Special:Search&quot;\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0d9b1f73f4554c3f\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5df59126887831d8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSuicides involving railways - Statistics | Eurostat\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5df59126887831d8\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/product/page/TRAN_SF_RAILSU\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b633ae91b497ba8a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWe cannot provide a description for this page right now\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b633ae91b497ba8a\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"33b08932be6841d8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n1 EUROSTAT 2019.27.06 Rail accident fatalities in the EU\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"33b08932be6841d8\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.sipotra.it/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Rail-accident-fatalities-in-the-EU.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ff3869ede32538bf\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe overall trends in the data show that railway travel is increasingly safe, with few fatalities among rail · passengers. The ERA estimated that for the period 2010-2014, the fatality risk for passengers travelling\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ff3869ede32538bf\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.sipotra.it\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f92f841da05521b7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTen-year incidence and time trends of railway suicides in Germany from 1991 to 2000 | European Journal of Public Health | Oxford Academic\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f92f841da05521b7\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://academic.oup.com/eurpub/article/16/2/173/505730\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3bcb4ee67419e656\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMethods: <strong>From 1991 to 2000, a total of 8653 fatal railway suicides were recorded by the national central registry of all passenger accidents on the German railway net. To assess time trends, the average annual percentage change (AAPC) of the number of suicides was estimated using Poisson regression</strong>...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3bcb4ee67419e656\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 1, 2006\",\n      \"siteName\": \"academic.oup.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"43d51b2893c863ee\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAssessment of the Impact of Rail Suicides on EU Railways\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"43d51b2893c863ee\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.era.europa.eu/system/files/2022-10/Report%20on%20assessment%20of%20the%20impact%20of%20rail%20suicides%20on%20EU%20railways.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1f8c0ac563b5ce54\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe European Union Agency for Railways (ERA) facilitates the development of the Single European Railway Area. It enhances interoperability, harmonises rules, and promotes safety. Since June 2019, ERA issues safety certificates and vehicle authorisations valid across multiple European countries.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1f8c0ac563b5ce54\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.era.europa.eu\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "Eurostat railway suicide statistics Germany 2014 2020 percentage decrease", "provider": "brave", "count": 10, "tookMs": 945, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"966e02073e573d33\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nRailway safety statistics in the EU Statistics Explained\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"966e02073e573d33\">>>", "url": "https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/SEPDF/cache/94376.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f44fa3ea9702bf83\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIt should be noted that there are no railways in the EU countries Cyprus and Malta, ... The number of significant railway accidents in the EU fell almost continuously between 2010 and 2020, with the · only exceptions being <strong>a sharp increase in 2014 (+6.7%)</strong> and a slight increase in 2017 (+2.1%).\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f44fa3ea9702bf83\">>>", "siteName": "ec.europa.eu"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6074532ab738f678\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nRail transport fatalities drop by 11% in 2024 - News articles - Eurostat\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6074532ab738f678\">>>", "url": "https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/products-eurostat-news/w/ddn-20251216-2", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c7655b89c5d67831\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe number of suicides on railways is constantly much higher than the number of fatalities despite the downward trend seen in the EU the past decade (2 357 in 2024 compared with 2 608 in 2014, <strong>-9.6%)</strong>.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c7655b89c5d67831\">>>", "published": "December 16, 2025", "siteName": "ec.europa.eu"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"bd14aa3d2803c6aa\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nRailway safety statistics in the EU - Statistics Explained - Eurostat\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"bd14aa3d2803c6aa\">>>", "url": "https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/index.php?title=Railway_safety_statistics_in_the_EU", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5a156a05cb234f3d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIt should be noted that there are no railways in the EU countries Cyprus and Malta, nor in the EEA/EFTA country Iceland. <strong>The number of significant railway accidents in the EU fell almost continuously between 2010 and 2020, with the only exceptions being a sharp increase in 2014</strong> ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5a156a05cb234f3d\">>>", "siteName": "ec.europa.eu"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0fee2667c1eadfa9\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nBehavioral and location‐related antecedents of train suicides - Moritz - 2023 - Suicide and Life-Threatening Behavior - Wiley Online Library\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0fee2667c1eadfa9\">>>", "url": "https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/sltb.12941", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b414cbf8f6d0acf8\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nA total of <strong>78.6% (n = 44) of the present sample were German nationals</strong>, which is somewhat lower than the proportion of individuals with German citizenship in Hamburg in 2020 (82.9%; Federal Statistical Office/Statistisches Bundesamt, 2021).\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b414cbf8f6d0acf8\">>>", "published": "January 30, 2023", "siteName": "onlinelibrary.wiley.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"66da31f50e87687c\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nEU railway deaths fall in 2024\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"66da31f50e87687c\">>>", "url": "https://www.globalrailwayreview.com/news/233725/railway-deaths-in-the-eu-fall-in-2024-after-years-of-fluctuating-trends/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5ba5c0898e672b83\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIn 2024, there were 2,357 suicides, <strong>down 9.6% from 2,608 in 2014.</strong> Germany recorded the highest number with 688, followed by France with 267 and the Netherlands with 186. The lowest numbers were observed in Lithuania with none, Greece with one, ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5ba5c0898e672b83\">>>", "published": "December 17, 2025", "siteName": "www.globalrailwayreview.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"20f999e02ba7d01c\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nSearch results for \"유로컵 참가국-（H87.CC）-유로컵 참가국->>h87.cc<<-h0neo.html\" - Statistics Explained - Eurostat\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"20f999e02ba7d01c\">>>", "url": "https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/index.php/Railway_safety_statistics_in_the_EU", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0d9b1f73f4554c3f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nRetrieved from &quot;https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/index.php?title=Special:Search&quot;\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0d9b1f73f4554c3f\">>>", "siteName": "ec.europa.eu"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5df59126887831d8\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nSuicides involving railways - Statistics | Eurostat\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5df59126887831d8\">>>", "url": "https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/product/page/TRAN_SF_RAILSU", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b633ae91b497ba8a\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nWe cannot provide a description for this page right now\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b633ae91b497ba8a\">>>", "siteName": "ec.europa.eu"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"33b08932be6841d8\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n1 EUROSTAT 2019.27.06 Rail accident fatalities in the EU\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"33b08932be6841d8\">>>", "url": "https://www.sipotra.it/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Rail-accident-fatalities-in-the-EU.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ff3869ede32538bf\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe overall trends in the data show that railway travel is increasingly safe, with few fatalities among rail · passengers. The ERA estimated that for the period 2010-2014, the fatality risk for passengers travelling\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ff3869ede32538bf\">>>", "siteName": "www.sipotra.it"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f92f841da05521b7\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTen-year incidence and time trends of railway suicides in Germany from 1991 to 2000 | European Journal of Public Health | Oxford Academic\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f92f841da05521b7\">>>", "url": "https://academic.oup.com/eurpub/article/16/2/173/505730", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3bcb4ee67419e656\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nMethods: <strong>From 1991 to 2000, a total of 8653 fatal railway suicides were recorded by the national central registry of all passenger accidents on the German railway net. To assess time trends, the average annual percentage change (AAPC) of the number of suicides was estimated using Poisson regression</strong>...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3bcb4ee67419e656\">>>", "published": "April 1, 2006", "siteName": "academic.oup.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"43d51b2893c863ee\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAssessment of the Impact of Rail Suicides on EU Railways\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"43d51b2893c863ee\">>>", "url": "https://www.era.europa.eu/system/files/2022-10/Report%20on%20assessment%20of%20the%20impact%20of%20rail%20suicides%20on%20EU%20railways.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1f8c0ac563b5ce54\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe European Union Agency for Railways (ERA) facilitates the development of the Single European Railway Area. It enhances interoperability, harmonises rules, and promotes safety. Since June 2019, ERA issues safety certificates and vehicle authorisations valid across multiple European countries.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1f8c0ac563b5ce54\">>>", "siteName": "www.era.europa.eu"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775818948868}}
