{"type": "message", "id": "d6e90485", "parentId": "72ee8c07", "timestamp": "2026-04-10T11:02:42.986Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "toolu_bdrk_012AV7Mt8uC1BBHi9sGfxoWH", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"Belgium railway suicides 2014 2020 decrease 45%\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 986,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a33b1224e0e249c5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSuicide on the Railways in Belgium: A Typology of Locations and Potential for Prevention - PMC\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a33b1224e0e249c5\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6209948/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d55b925763267287\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSince 2012, Infrabel has built an action plan against suicide on the railway network [24]. This action plan is based on a multi-step approach designed in the Campaigns and Awareness Raising Strategies in Traffic Safety project [25] and comprises six steps and their subsequent actions. This approach was also used in the 2011–2014 Reduction of Suicides and Trespasses on Railway property (RESTRAIL) project led by the International Union of Railways [15]. Implemented preventive measures include the installation of fences in open railway lines, establishing collaboration with the psychiatric facilities nearby the railways, installation of blue lights in hotspots stations, installation of intelligent thermal cameras, and poster campaigns at railway stations [24]. All these measures will be evaluated over the next years.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d55b925763267287\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"904e0e7497f0f59d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nStrategies for Reducing Suicide at Railroads: A Scoping Review of Evidence and Gaps - PMC\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"904e0e7497f0f59d\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11765353/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5b5c0e9490c801f1\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThis review aims to systematically evaluate existing literature on reducing suicides along railroads, with specific focus on effectiveness, limitations, and research gaps in the current evidence base. Database searches were conducted in PubMed, ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5b5c0e9490c801f1\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2f0993c5459c5087\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nFull article: Environmental Risk Factors for Railway Suicide: A Nationwide Analysis of England’s Mainline Network (2019–2021)\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2f0993c5459c5087\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/13811118.2025.2595428\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b756bd6a8ef975ff\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe extent to which deaths are concentrated in identifiable clusters or ‘hotspots’ also varies widely, from 0% in Canada to 17% in Austria, 30% in Chicago, and <strong>35% in Belgium and Australia</strong> (Mishara &amp; Bardon, Citation2016, Citation2017; Savage, ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b756bd6a8ef975ff\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.tandfonline.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9645b0f987ca6ea2\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<span class=\\\"mw-page-title-main\\\">Railway safety statistics in the EU</span>\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9645b0f987ca6ea2\\\"